Directory for SPECTER builds using CMake

To compile from this directory, do:
cmake ..
make

You can also build in parallel using, e.g., "make -j4".

If libraries are not in the path, use -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH and -DFFTW3_ROOT to
set paths, e.g., from this directory do:

cmake .. -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/foo/openmpi-5.0.8 -DFFTW3_ROOT=/foo/fftw-3.3.10
make

Executables are generated by default in SPECTER/bin. You can install SPECTER in
a different directory using:

cmake .. -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/foo
make
make install

The shell scripts in this directory are not needed for compilation, but provide
examples on how to compile SPECTER with different configurations (host only,
amd offloading, and nvidia offloading with LLVM or NVIDIA compilers). Each one
builds in its own subdirectory (build/host, build/amd and build/nvidia-llvm or
build/nvidia-nvhpc), takes the precision as an argument, and leaves the
executables in bin, bin/amd and bin/nvidia.
